\intbl {\f0 {\f0\fs20 {\super \i 1} Raw-unit regression coefficients; *** p < .001, ** p < .01, * p < .05. "--" marks a predictor the model does not contain. Raw coefficients are not comparable across predictors on different scales -- see the 07 output folder for standardized betas and confidence intervals.\line {\super \i 2} Both drug groups are fit in ONE model, with drug as a predictor. Drug is a factor with Hydrocodone group as reference, so every drug row reads Tramadol group minus Hydrocodone group. In P2 the plain receptor and ROE rows are that predictor's slope in Hydrocodone group; add the matching interaction row to get Tramadol group. P1 vs P2 is the test of whether the two drugs share slopes at all -- see the section 20 output folder for that F test and for each drug's derived slope. "model p" is the overall F test for that column's model.}}\cell

